 "answer_type": "expression",
 "context": null,
 "params": [
  {
   "name": "p",
   "randint": [
    1,
    6
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "q",
   "randint": [
    1,
    6
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "c",
   "randint": [
    1,
    5
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "d",
   "randint": [
    1,
    5
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "A",
   "let": "p * c + q * d"
  },
  {
   "name": "B",
   "let": "q * c - p * d"
  },
  {
   "require": "B > 0",
   "why": "imaginary part of numerator positive so it prints cleanly"
  },
  {
   "name": "N",
   "let": "c * c + d * d"
  }
 ],
 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Write $\\dfrac{ {=A} + {=B}i}{ {=c} - {=d}i}$ in the form $a + bi$.",
 "answer": "",
 "solution": [
  "The conjugate of the denominator ${=c}-{=d}i$ is ${=c}+{=d}i$. Multiply numerator and denominator by it: $\\dfrac{({=A}+{=B}i)({=c}+{=d}i)}{({=c}-{=d}i)({=c}+{=d}i)}$.",
  "Denominator: $({=c}-{=d}i)({=c}+{=d}i)={=c*c}-{=d*d}i^2={=c*c}+{=d*d}={=N}$.",
  "Numerator: $({=A}+{=B}i)({=c}+{=d}i)={=A*c}+{=A*d}i+{=B*c}i+{=B*d}i^2=({=A*c}-{=B*d})+({=A*d}+{=B*c})i={=N*p}+{=N*q}i$.",
  "Divide by ${=N}$: $\\dfrac{ {=N*p}+{=N*q}i}{ {=N}}={=p}+{=q}i$."
 ],
 "marker": {
  "kind": "expression",
  "answer": "{=p} + {=q}*i",
  "form": null,
  "variables": [
   "i"
  ],
  "tolerance": null
 },
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Numerator built as (p+qi)(c-di) so the quotient is the whole-number complex p+qi; the conjugate of the divisor is c+di. Requires q*c-p*d>0 so the numerator prints as A + Bi."
}
